-- Regulations 1 to 5 and 10 of the Income Tax (Deduction from Salary and Wages) Regulations 5753-1993: which
-- payments of salary the employer deducts from, and how, as far as the deduction is from a monthly salary.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/regulations/income-tax-deduction-from-salary-and-wages-regulations-5753-1993.he.wiki.txt
-- (sha256 e6fd6975...b7b20f). Regulation 1 is lines 14-43; 2: 45-52; 3: 54-60; 4: 62-65; 5: 67-74; 10: 132-133.
-- References to the Ordinance below name a section, not a line, because `src:` comments in this file quote
-- the Regulations only.

§ `Regulations 1 to 5 and 10 — the deduction from a month's salary`

§§ `Regulation 1 — the definitions the deduction turns on`

-- src:19 | ”עובד יומי“ – יחיד המקבל שכר עבודה ממעביד אחד בעד עבודה של פחות משמונה עשר ימים בחודש, אולם לא פחות משמונה שעות בשבוע;
-- src:28 | ”משכורת חודש“ – משכורת המשולמת לעובד בעד עבודת חודש: לענין זה, ”עבודת חודש“ – למעט עבודה של פחות מ־18 ימים בחודש:
-- src:29 | ”משכורת חלקית“ – משכורת המשולמת לעובד בעד עבודה של חמש שעות ליום או פחות, או בעד עבודה של יותר מחמש שעות ליום, אולם פחות משמונה שעות בשבוע;
-- src:32 | ”משכורת בעד משרה נוספת“ – משכורת המשולמת לעובד בעד עבודה של יותר מחמש שעות ביום, המועסק במקום עבודה אחר או המקבל ממעביד אחר קצבה חייבת במס;
@ref Regulations 5753-1993, reg 1 "עובד יומי", "משכורת חלקית" (source lines 19, 29)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `A payment of salary`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payment is a partial salary or a pension` `the payment` MEANS
        `the payment`'s `the payment is a pension`
    OR  `the payment`'s `hours worked a day` AT MOST 5
    OR  (`the payment`'s `hours worked a day` GREATER THAN 5 AND `the payment`'s `hours worked a week` LESS THAN 8)

-- A day employee: wages from one employer for work of fewer than 18 days in the month, but not fewer than eight
-- hours a week. (A person who is within the partial-salary definition is dealt with first, by regulation 5.)
@ref Regulations 5753-1993, reg 1 "עובד יומי" (source line 19)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `A payment of salary`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payment is wages of a day employee` `the payment` MEANS
        `the payment`'s `days worked in the month` LESS THAN 18
    AND `the payment`'s `hours worked a week` AT LEAST 8

-- A salary for an additional position: more than five hours a day, the employee employed elsewhere or
-- receiving a taxable pension from another payer. Regulation 5(a) deducts at the maximal rate from one that
-- the employee declared on the card.
@ref Regulations 5753-1993, reg 1 "משכורת בעד משרה נוספת" (source line 32); reg 5(a) (source line 68)
GIVEN `the payment`      IS A `A payment of salary`
      `the declarations` IS AN `The employee's declarations`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payment is a salary for an additional position that the employee declared` `the payment` `given` `the declarations` MEANS
        `the payment`'s `hours worked a day` GREATER THAN 5
    AND `the payment`'s `the employee works elsewhere, or receives a taxable pension from another payer`
    AND `the declarations`'s `declared on the card an additional position, or a taxable pension from another payer`

